# Copy to /etc/restic/b2.env on pve-prod, chmod 600, root-owned. NEVER commit.
# Its presence is what switches copy 3 on - restic-backup.sh skips the B2 step
# entirely when this file is absent, so the jjserver half works without it.
#
# ── Creating the account ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   https://www.backblaze.com/sign-up/cloud-storage
#
# ⚠️ CHOOSE THE **EU CENTRAL** REGION (Amsterdam) AT SIGNUP.
# B2 offers US West, US East, EU Central and Canada East at identical prices,
# and the region is fixed when the account is created - it cannot be changed
# later. From South Africa, Amsterdam is roughly 150-180 ms against 250-300 ms
# to US West. Same money, half the latency.
#
# ── Creating the key ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# B2 Cloud Storage > Application Keys > Add a New Application Key.
# Do NOT use the master key. Scope a standard key to this one bucket, so a
# leaked credential cannot touch anything else in the account.
# The applicationKey is displayed exactly once. Copy it immediately.
#
# ── Cost ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# USD 6.95 per TB per month, billed per GB with no minimum. About 182 GB is
# backed up here, so roughly USD 1.30/month. Egress is free up to three times
# what is stored (about 546 GB/month), so a full restore costs nothing.
# Above ~500 GB stored, a flat-rate provider such as Hetzner Storage Box
# becomes cheaper - `restic copy` moves between backends keeping history.

B2_ACCOUNT_ID=<keyID from the application key>
B2_ACCOUNT_KEY=<applicationKey, shown only once>

# Bucket must already exist and should be PRIVATE. restic encrypts client-side
# regardless, but a public bucket leaks object names and sizes.
B2_REPOSITORY=b2:<bucket-name>:/pve-prod

# The B2 repo uses the SAME password as the jjserver repo (/etc/restic/password).
# `restic copy` requires it, and one password for both halves is one thing to
# lose rather than two.
